The last three reruns are still going; I'll put the full comparison together when they finish. Two results are already clear from the sets that are complete.

**The multi-call change works live.** In the build with the change, the model asked for 123 tool calls across twelve conversations, sometimes several in one reply (17 times), and all 123 were carried out. In the old build on the same conversations, the model asked for 144 and only 123 happened. The other 21 were silently dropped.

**With deferral reversed, the preparation finishes when nothing else gets in the way.** In three of the six fitting conversations finished so far, the assistant went all the way:

- recorded what the part is for;
- found PETG in the printer's own preset list and switched to it;
- set the build plate once told which one is installed;
- chose a stronger process setting or raised the walls and infill;
- sliced, and read the slice report.

The other three were stopped by the slicing bug I put the task chip up for: the slice tool says it started when nothing was sliced, then hangs on the retry. None of the six ended because of a refused tool call. With deferral on, every fitting conversation ended that way, and none ever reached a slice.

